WEBVTT

00:02.336 --> 00:04.632
<i>♪ it seems today
 that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.676 --> 00:07.680
<i>♪ is violence in movies
 and sex on tv ♪</i>

00:07.807 --> 00:11.355
<i>♪ but where are those
 good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.441 --> 00:14.363
<i>♪ on which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.449 --> 00:17.996
<i>♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.082 --> 00:21.296
<i>♪ lucky there's a man who
 positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.423 --> 00:22.924
<i>♪ all the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.010 --> 00:24.135
<i>♪ laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.262 --> 00:30.192
<i>♪ he's... A...
 Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:36.166 --> 00:37.333
There you are, peter.

00:37.460 --> 00:39.171
Help me hang the stockings.

00:39.298 --> 00:41.760
Not now, lois. It's time
for my favorite holiday movie,

00:41.804 --> 00:43.097
<i> Frosty the snowman,</i>

00:43.225 --> 00:45.477
Where a hero takes a little girl
into the woods

00:45.604 --> 00:49.069
And then brags that he
can disappear whenever he wants.

00:51.327 --> 00:53.621
Huh. I can't see the tv.

00:53.748 --> 00:54.959
I must be dreaming.

00:55.044 --> 00:56.837
Which means nothing's real!

00:57.005 --> 00:58.968
-[grunting]
-[gasps, groaning]

00:59.053 --> 01:01.348
No, peter, stop!
You're not dreaming!

01:01.433 --> 01:03.478
<i>Yeah, and why was that
your first move?</i>

01:03.564 --> 01:05.732
The tv's gone.
We're cutting the cord.

01:05.818 --> 01:08.239
We need money for
christmas gifts, so I sold it.

01:08.324 --> 01:12.374
What?! This rageful anger
calls for alcohol!

01:12.459 --> 01:13.419
[gulping]

01:13.504 --> 01:14.378
Where's brian?

01:14.463 --> 01:15.422
Peter, stop it.

01:15.549 --> 01:17.178
What am I supposed to do
without a tv?

01:17.263 --> 01:18.638
Hang out at the gap?

01:18.724 --> 01:21.103
Could you please point me
to your blandest shirt?

01:21.230 --> 01:23.734
One that I'm guaranteed
to see four other guys wearing

01:23.819 --> 01:25.070
Before I even get to my car.

01:25.239 --> 01:26.616
Sure, it's right over there.

01:26.659 --> 01:27.910
Just be careful
while you're browsing

01:28.037 --> 01:30.750
That you don't lose track
of which white guy is you.

01:31.712 --> 01:33.381
Oh, that looks good on me.

01:33.425 --> 01:35.136
<i>[announcer]
the gap, the only clothing store</i>

01:35.222 --> 01:36.138
<i> Named for a taint.</i>

01:36.224 --> 01:37.350
<i> Located between vera wang</i>

01:37.435 --> 01:39.229
<i> And the rocky mountain
 chocolate factory.</i>

01:39.314 --> 01:41.275
Look, I know
this seems like a big change,

01:41.319 --> 01:43.363
But we don't need
a television anymore.

01:43.448 --> 01:46.162
Yeah, dad.
A single tv console is outdated.

01:46.206 --> 01:48.709
Everyone just streams now
on their individual devices.

01:48.836 --> 01:52.385
Who is this person who speaks
to me as if I needed his advice?

01:52.470 --> 01:55.475
Dad, I'm just trying to bring
you into the modern era.

01:55.560 --> 01:57.145
I see.

01:59.069 --> 02:00.152
[screaming]

02:00.281 --> 02:01.698
-[splat]
-[man] quiet up there!

02:01.826 --> 02:04.079
Sorry! Just demonstrating
I'm still relevant

02:04.164 --> 02:06.166
By making
a very old movie reference!

02:06.336 --> 02:07.796
Peter, meg was right.

02:07.881 --> 02:10.886
We don't need a tv
in the golden age of streaming.

02:10.972 --> 02:12.264
"golden age of streaming"?

02:12.349 --> 02:14.019
Look, my streams are sporadic
at best.

02:14.104 --> 02:15.522
And last week, there was blood.

02:15.649 --> 02:19.198
Can we have one holiday where
we don't discuss dad's rod?

02:19.326 --> 02:21.453
Besides, all my shows
are on network television.

02:21.580 --> 02:23.834
<i>How the hell am I supposed
to watch chicago fire</i>

02:23.919 --> 02:25.463
-Without a tv?
-Who cares?

02:25.590 --> 02:27.300
It's a lazy, formulaic show.

02:27.385 --> 02:29.305
And it's not even filmed
in chicago.

02:29.390 --> 02:30.807
Yeah, right.
Tell that to the boys

02:30.934 --> 02:32.187
Putting out a blaze this week

02:32.272 --> 02:33.773
In the famed chicago hills.

02:33.901 --> 02:36.237
It almost burned down
the chicagowood sign!

02:36.323 --> 02:37.406
Peter, stop it.

02:37.533 --> 02:39.078
God, you're going in circles,

02:39.163 --> 02:40.790
Like a desert vulture.

02:40.875 --> 02:42.878
Hey, maybe we shouldn't
always fly in a circle.

02:43.005 --> 02:45.927
Sure. And maybe I can also have
rough sex with your mother.

02:46.012 --> 02:47.346
Whoa! Come on.

02:47.432 --> 02:49.977
Well, that's how I feel
about your idea.

02:53.571 --> 02:55.741
<i>[announcer] we now return
 to frosty the snowman.</i>

02:55.868 --> 02:59.083
<i> There was indeed some magic
 in that old silk hat,</i>

02:59.168 --> 03:01.338
<i> Along with duct tape, zip ties</i>

03:01.465 --> 03:03.260
<i> And some very troubling
 polaroids.</i>

03:03.345 --> 03:05.139
See? This is the kind
of wholesome stuff

03:05.224 --> 03:06.434
I'll miss without a tv.

03:06.561 --> 03:09.399
Lois is right, peter.
Network television stinks.

03:09.527 --> 03:11.111
Streaming is
way more entertaining.

03:11.196 --> 03:13.367
Yeah? Name one good show
on "streaming."

03:13.453 --> 03:14.494
<i> Mare of easttown!</i>

03:14.663 --> 03:16.123
<i> -Fargo!
 -True detective.</i>

03:16.208 --> 03:18.044
<i> -American rust!
 -Broadchurch.</i>

03:18.130 --> 03:20.592
That isn't about a person
attempting to navigate life

03:20.719 --> 03:23.098
In a small town
in the aftermath of a murder.

03:24.101 --> 03:26.481
Look, come on, just-just give
streaming a chance.

03:26.566 --> 03:27.941
Don't you want
to watch something where,

03:28.028 --> 03:30.991
If you miss even a second,
you're hopelessly confused?

03:31.076 --> 03:33.321
Yeah! Or a great premise,

03:33.373 --> 03:35.210
Which puts a lot of balls
in the air,

03:35.337 --> 03:37.413
Followed by
a horribly disappointing ending

03:37.466 --> 03:38.635
That drops all of them?

03:38.720 --> 03:39.803
And on hbo max,

03:39.889 --> 03:41.182
Sometimes after the credits,

03:41.267 --> 03:43.187
You can watch
the actors talk about the show.

03:43.231 --> 03:46.568
Yeah, I don't just want to see
connie britton do a good job.

03:46.655 --> 03:48.324
<i>I want to see
connie britton talking</i>

03:48.368 --> 03:50.244
About the good job she just did.

03:50.330 --> 03:51.748
You know
what I'm not hearing, guys?

03:51.833 --> 03:54.003
Cedric the entertainer
telling a white guy

03:54.130 --> 03:55.465
That he doesn't walk
the right way.

03:55.635 --> 03:59.098
Hmm. I may have to side
with peter now.

03:59.183 --> 04:00.185
And you also haven't told me

04:00.271 --> 04:01.729
About a single show
with sheldon.

04:01.815 --> 04:03.694
For every program,
I want to know,

04:03.821 --> 04:04.862
Is there a sheldon

04:04.990 --> 04:06.449
And at what stage of life is he?

04:06.618 --> 04:09.373
He is the perfect dumb guy's
version of a smart guy.

04:09.458 --> 04:11.335
And I demand him
on my television!

04:11.462 --> 04:14.885
All right. I think I see
how to untangle this knot.

04:14.971 --> 04:16.724
<i> Last tango in halifax.</i>

04:16.851 --> 04:18.645
<i>-What?
-You've never heard of tango?</i>

04:18.731 --> 04:22.070
Well, anne reid and derek jacobi
play celia and alan,

04:22.197 --> 04:26.413
A couple reunited in their 70s
after 60 years apart.

04:26.457 --> 04:29.462
Sarah lancashire plays
celia's formidable daughter,

04:29.547 --> 04:30.464
Caroline. And n--

04:30.591 --> 04:32.260
-[screams]
-[splat]

04:32.346 --> 04:36.353
Look, guys, I j-- I don't like
gritty, convoluted television.

04:36.480 --> 04:39.903
I like the simple,
comforting joy of network tv.

04:39.988 --> 04:42.368
Peter, the point of tv
isn't joy anymore.

04:42.453 --> 04:44.372
It's to destroy you emotionally.

04:44.457 --> 04:46.043
Who the hell wants
to watch something happy

04:46.128 --> 04:48.297
When you can watch
koreans fight to the death?

04:48.383 --> 04:51.347
Well, I disagree. And I'm not
letting lois get away with this.

04:51.474 --> 04:52.724
'cause I miss my shows.

04:52.810 --> 04:54.396
<i>Like the comedy of black-ish</i>

04:54.481 --> 04:56.567
Or those classic
new york conversations

04:56.653 --> 04:58.071
<i>At the beginning of law & order.</i>

04:58.198 --> 05:00.660
Hey, you see that aaron judge
baseball hit last night?

05:00.787 --> 05:03.793
Sure did. Right here
in one of our five boroughs.

05:03.878 --> 05:05.087
Oh, no!

05:05.172 --> 05:08.637
I bet you a slice
of new york pizza pie he's dead!

05:12.774 --> 05:15.946
I can't believe you buy
milk and bras at the same place.

05:16.073 --> 05:17.282
God, we're trash.

05:17.410 --> 05:18.828
What? Where's the fridge?

05:18.914 --> 05:21.250
<i>I sold it. You get rid
of the things I love,</i>

05:21.335 --> 05:22.837
I get rid
of the things you love.

05:22.922 --> 05:25.927
I also sold that tiny jewish hat
you keep in the bathroom.

05:26.054 --> 05:27.557
That was my diaphragm.

05:27.642 --> 05:30.313
Ah. Well, mort's gonna have
a rough day at temple.

05:30.482 --> 05:32.359
Look, just give streaming
a shot.

05:32.529 --> 05:33.738
After all, it can't be any worse

05:33.823 --> 05:35.826
Than when we went
to the florida panhandle.

05:35.953 --> 05:39.835
<i>Mmm. Ah, this shrimp
is delicious. [chuckles]</i>

05:39.879 --> 05:41.507
[gasps, choking]

05:41.592 --> 05:43.134
Oh, god, my wife's choking!

05:43.261 --> 05:45.057
Is there a doctor in the house?!

05:45.142 --> 05:46.977
College graduate?

05:47.063 --> 05:48.523
High school graduate?

05:49.485 --> 05:51.320
Some high school
with vocational degree?

05:52.282 --> 05:55.079
Whoever gets the shrimp out
of her windpipe can have it!

05:55.165 --> 05:57.085
[screaming, shouting]

06:01.137 --> 06:03.808
Well, I guess it's time
to try this streaming thing.

06:03.936 --> 06:05.605
Hey, what's
our netflix password?

06:05.732 --> 06:07.818
Uh, I don't know.
I use quagmire's.

06:08.487 --> 06:09.906
<i> Squirrel hunter?</i>

06:09.992 --> 06:12.662
<i> The truth about kicking
 your leg during sleep?</i>

06:12.790 --> 06:15.545
<i> Only the otis scenes
 of milo and otis?</i>

06:15.672 --> 06:18.260
<i>And thirsty romanian coeds.
All right!</i>

06:18.345 --> 06:19.470
We do have some overlap.

06:19.598 --> 06:22.769
Okay, I guess
I'll click "forgot password."

06:22.898 --> 06:25.601
Now it's asking me to pick
all the stoplights in a picture.

06:25.653 --> 06:27.824
Huh. A stoplight
in front of a movie theater

06:27.951 --> 06:30.203
<i>With a marquee
reading spotlight.</i>

06:30.289 --> 06:31.625
This might be a trick.

06:31.710 --> 06:34.840
All right, "what is
the first concert you attended?"

06:34.926 --> 06:38.139
"smash mouth, the time
they got bread thrown at them."

06:38.224 --> 06:39.809
"favorite pet?"

06:39.937 --> 06:42.315
Wait, you're not gonna write
"bartholomew," are you?

06:42.400 --> 06:43.653
No, no, no.
I would never do that.

06:43.780 --> 06:45.782
<i>♪ bartholomew, bartholomew ♪</i>

06:45.909 --> 06:49.122
<i>♪ I'm dancing with
my favorite dog, bartholomew! ♪</i>

06:49.250 --> 06:50.752
[knocking]

06:51.631 --> 06:52.799
Kevin james?!

06:52.926 --> 06:55.514
Hi, peter. You were
my last viewer. [chuckles]

06:55.599 --> 06:57.643
And now that you've gotten rid
of network tv,

06:57.728 --> 06:58.895
I'm out of a job.

06:59.023 --> 07:00.567
Well, you're a sitcom dad,

07:00.653 --> 07:03.115
So if the couch accepts you,
you can come in.

07:06.249 --> 07:07.165
[screams]

07:07.292 --> 07:09.505
[giggles]
road couch.

07:14.686 --> 07:16.438
Wow! Kevin james!

07:16.481 --> 07:17.648
I can't believe you're here!

07:17.860 --> 07:19.193
Hey, guys, we got company!

07:19.320 --> 07:20.572
No nude wandering!

07:20.658 --> 07:23.495
Well, so much
for full frontal fridays.

07:23.581 --> 07:25.710
Wait, triple "f" is a no-go?

07:25.837 --> 07:28.257
Look, I'm here
because now that I don't have

07:28.342 --> 07:30.211
Any viewers or a job,

07:30.305 --> 07:32.141
I need you to take care of me.

07:32.268 --> 07:33.311
What, is that some kind of rule?

07:33.480 --> 07:34.647
Of course it is, lois.

07:34.775 --> 07:37.196
In network tv, if someone
shows up at your door,

07:37.281 --> 07:38.364
You have to take care of 'em.

07:38.408 --> 07:39.742
It's the pilot of most shows.

07:39.828 --> 07:41.747
Oh, really? Name 50.

07:41.832 --> 07:43.585
<i> New girl, two and a half men,</i>

07:43.670 --> 07:45.463
<i> Punky brewster,
 perfect strangers,</i>

07:45.591 --> 07:46.759
<i> Frasier, will & grace,</i>

07:46.844 --> 07:48.805
<i> Friends, joey, home economics,</i>

07:48.890 --> 07:50.768
<i> Mom, dads, cheers,</i>

07:50.854 --> 07:52.481
<i> Hope & faith, raising hope,</i>

07:52.566 --> 07:53.858
<i> Full house, fuller house,</i>

07:54.028 --> 07:55.529
<i> -King of queens--
-that's good.</i>

07:55.657 --> 07:56.824
-I-I think we get it.
-Oh, no, no.

07:56.951 --> 07:59.205
No, this is
a "name all 50" kind of show.

07:59.290 --> 08:01.334
<i> Too close for comfort,
 mork & mindy,</i>

08:01.378 --> 08:03.047
<i> The nanny, mr. Belvedere,</i>

08:03.133 --> 08:05.136
<i> The united states of al,
 yes, dear,</i>

08:05.221 --> 08:07.683
<i> Down and out in beverly hills,
the tv series,</i>

08:07.810 --> 08:09.228
<i> Rhoda, golden girls,</i>

08:09.355 --> 08:11.442
<i> Alf, meego, empty nest,</i>

08:11.570 --> 08:12.778
<i> Wings, my two dads,</i>

08:12.864 --> 08:14.783
<i> Evening shade,
 I dream of jeannie,</i>

08:14.910 --> 08:16.495
<i> Off centre, webster,</i>

08:16.622 --> 08:18.876
<i> The bernie mac show,
 the return of jezebel james,</i>

08:19.003 --> 08:21.299
<i> Aliens in america,
 last man on earth,</i>

08:21.384 --> 08:22.843
<i> Union square, bram & alice,</i>

08:22.928 --> 08:24.849
<i>The grinder, bleep my dad says,</i>

08:24.934 --> 08:26.393
<i> The fresh prince of bel-air,</i>

08:26.478 --> 08:27.814
<i> Damon, happy endings,</i>

08:27.900 --> 08:29.650
<i> Big brother jake,
 three's company,</i>

08:29.736 --> 08:31.572
<i> Mama's family
and who's the boss?</i>

08:31.700 --> 08:33.995
Oh, yeah? Name 50 more.

08:34.080 --> 08:35.414
[sighs heavily]

08:35.499 --> 08:37.252
<i> Silver spoons, the odd couple,</i>

08:37.338 --> 08:38.504
<i> The new odd couple...</i>

08:38.590 --> 08:39.799
<i> -Diff'rent strokes and--
-[creaking]</i>

08:39.969 --> 08:42.389
Oh, my god! She hung herself!

08:42.433 --> 08:43.643
<i>Nah, nah, that's from airplane.</i>

08:43.811 --> 08:45.188
We do that kind of stuff, too.

08:45.315 --> 08:46.733
You can stay.

08:49.909 --> 08:52.237
Family, meet kevin.

08:52.289 --> 08:53.624
Wow!

08:53.710 --> 08:56.088
I guess black dress shirts
aren't just for magicians.

08:56.216 --> 08:59.554
[quietly] peter, you can't
just invite him to stay here.

08:59.640 --> 09:01.560
Come on, lois.
When you got rid of the tv,

09:01.646 --> 09:02.938
Did you really think
it wouldn't end

09:03.023 --> 09:04.775
With me bunking
with kevin james?

09:04.860 --> 09:07.615
So, kevin,
what's mandy patinkin like?

09:07.701 --> 09:09.537
Uh, I don't know. Never met him.

09:09.622 --> 09:12.126
I thought you said
this guy was a [bleep] star.

09:12.211 --> 09:13.964
Hey, brian, when are you going
to try to impress

09:14.133 --> 09:16.428
Our hollywood guest
with your writerly chops?

09:16.513 --> 09:19.226
Uh, your mouth's moving!
You're already rehearsing it.

09:19.312 --> 09:22.233
So, kevin, the hollywood game
can be pretty tough, huh?

09:22.277 --> 09:24.447
Do you have
hollywood experience?

09:24.574 --> 09:26.452
[chuckling]
well, actually--

09:26.579 --> 09:28.247
He sure does!
We went out there once,

09:28.333 --> 09:30.210
And on day one,
brian bit a culkin.

09:30.296 --> 09:32.298
Tried to pet him
without showing his hand first

09:32.383 --> 09:33.676
And, boom, fingers gone.

09:33.845 --> 09:34.888
I need to see the hand!

09:34.973 --> 09:36.350
It's how I know
he's not an aggressor.

09:36.435 --> 09:37.936
Kevin, I don't understand.

09:38.064 --> 09:39.441
How can you be out of work?

09:39.610 --> 09:41.194
You're not just
a television actor--

09:41.279 --> 09:42.655
You're a movie star!

09:42.741 --> 09:44.786
Movie star?
[chuckles] come on.

09:44.871 --> 09:47.626
<i>I mean, I guess
paul blart did make 200 million</i>

09:47.753 --> 09:49.130
On a shoestring budget,

09:49.257 --> 09:51.552
<i>I was the single most bankable
comedy actor</i>

09:51.638 --> 09:53.181
Of the last two decades

09:53.266 --> 09:56.438
<i>And the audience score on
grown ups was very respectable.</i>

09:56.565 --> 09:59.320
Eh, the last one doesn't seem to
measure up with the first two.

09:59.406 --> 10:03.246
But everything I had was because
people knew me from network tv.

10:03.373 --> 10:04.750
And now that's over.

10:04.919 --> 10:07.004
So, peter, what are we gonna do
after dinner?

10:07.090 --> 10:08.634
Get a large bowl of popcorn

10:08.761 --> 10:11.640
And watch the big game
in our sports uniforms?

10:11.810 --> 10:13.061
Yeah, kevin, uh, I think

10:13.147 --> 10:15.692
You've only watched
sporting events on tv shows.

10:15.819 --> 10:17.196
Nobody calls it "the big game"

10:17.282 --> 10:19.367
Or makes
a large bowl of popcorn.

10:19.453 --> 10:21.164
But then what's gonna fly
all over the place

10:21.249 --> 10:22.875
-When we get excited?
-[giggles]

10:22.960 --> 10:24.713
Okay. A-all right, all right,
that's fair.

10:24.840 --> 10:26.886
All right, look,
kevin can stay for dinner,

10:26.971 --> 10:28.054
But then he has to leave.

10:28.140 --> 10:29.726
But he doesn't have
anywhere else to go!

10:29.811 --> 10:31.312
And this whole thing
is our fault.

10:31.439 --> 10:33.233
Come on, look at him--
he's got no idea

10:33.320 --> 10:35.488
What life outside of sitcoms
is like.

10:35.574 --> 10:38.496
<i>I tell you what-- I'll show him
how to be a real real guy</i>

10:38.623 --> 10:40.500
And not just a sitcom real guy,

10:40.628 --> 10:42.339
And then he'll be on his way.

10:42.466 --> 10:43.883
[sighs]
fine.

10:44.010 --> 10:45.972
I guess I can't kick someone out
on christmas.

10:46.099 --> 10:47.934
But where's he gonna sleep?

10:48.102 --> 10:49.813
Don't worry.
I got that all figured out.

10:49.941 --> 10:51.818
You won't even notice
he's there.

10:51.988 --> 10:54.198
-[snoring]
-[canned laughter]

10:56.164 --> 10:58.835
In network tv,
what someone says won't happen,

10:58.921 --> 11:00.463
That's what's gonna happen.

11:00.590 --> 11:02.385
[canned laughter]

11:08.610 --> 11:09.986
Hey, where's kevin?
I thought we were gonna show him

11:10.071 --> 11:11.115
How regular guys drink.

11:11.284 --> 11:12.826
We are, but he's still
adjusting,

11:12.869 --> 11:14.747
And he won't enter a room
until his warm-up guy

11:14.791 --> 11:15.782
Works the crowd.

11:15.877 --> 11:17.754
-So, where you folks from?
-Quahog.

11:17.840 --> 11:19.132
[chuckles] oh, quahog.

11:19.217 --> 11:20.887
I'll talk a little slower.

11:20.973 --> 11:22.890
-Aw, he got me.
-I'm just kidding.

11:22.976 --> 11:25.063
And, hey, thank you
for your service.

11:25.190 --> 11:26.734
Oh, I was never in the military.

11:26.819 --> 11:29.239
I was talking to the booth
holding you up.

11:29.367 --> 11:32.372
Oh, damn it, he got me again!
This guy's too quick.

11:32.500 --> 11:34.418
All right, everyone, kevin's
gonna be out in a moment,

11:34.503 --> 11:37.468
So remember,
he feeds off your energy.

11:37.553 --> 11:40.725
So the better you are,
the better kevin's gonna be.

11:40.852 --> 11:43.189
Hi, guys.
Great to see you tonight.

11:44.193 --> 11:46.322
Wait, he couldn't just
think of that?

11:46.449 --> 11:49.537
And doesn't peter griffin
look handsome?

11:49.623 --> 11:51.376
I took the cue cards.

11:51.503 --> 11:53.923
I grabbed him
from behind too hard,

11:54.050 --> 11:55.551
And now he's not moving.

11:58.352 --> 12:00.396
Hey, kevin, was that lady
always pressuring you

12:00.481 --> 12:01.733
To join scientology?

12:01.819 --> 12:04.489
No. I'm a devout catholic,
and that's even weirder.

12:04.616 --> 12:07.121
Did you know that when
unbaptized babies die,

12:07.248 --> 12:09.710
They go into limbo
until the pope said

12:09.795 --> 12:11.214
That wasn't a thing anymore?

12:11.341 --> 12:14.346
Yeah, my grandpa went to hell
for eating meat on fridays.

12:15.976 --> 12:17.687
Worth it.

12:20.529 --> 12:22.238
Well, kevin,
it's time to teach you

12:22.324 --> 12:25.663
How real blue-collar guys
pay real bills in real life.

12:25.790 --> 12:27.544
See this? It's a mortgage bill.

12:27.713 --> 12:29.757
And this is how it gets paid.

12:29.842 --> 12:31.470
Mr. Pewterschmidt, it's peter.

12:31.555 --> 12:33.933
<i>-Please pay my mortgage.
-[carter] damn it, griffin!</i>

12:34.019 --> 12:36.105
I'm crying, mr. Pewterschmidt,
I'm crying.

12:36.232 --> 12:38.109
<i> I know you're crying.
 Act like a man.</i>

12:38.195 --> 12:40.574
I can't. I'm not a man.
And if you don't pay it,

12:40.618 --> 12:43.038
I'm gonna hurt myself
and your grandchildren.

12:43.123 --> 12:45.294
<i> -Stop threatening me.
-It's not a threat if I do it.</i>

12:45.421 --> 12:47.130
It's not a threat if I do it.

12:47.216 --> 12:49.178
<i> -Okay, okay, I'll pay it.
-Thank you.</i>

12:49.305 --> 12:52.477
All right, now to show you
how to pay a utility bill.

12:52.562 --> 12:53.854
[phone ringing]

12:53.941 --> 12:56.152
-Hello?
-Kevin, it's peter.

12:56.238 --> 12:58.407
I really messed up, man.

13:01.918 --> 13:04.589
Good news.
I got my first real job

13:04.758 --> 13:06.259
As an actual ups guy.

13:06.386 --> 13:08.055
They said I was
the last non-robot

13:08.182 --> 13:09.517
They're ever gonna hire.

13:09.686 --> 13:10.895
That's great, buddy.

13:11.022 --> 13:12.984
You narrowly escaped
becoming a realtor.

13:13.069 --> 13:16.031
Hi. Are you the realtor
for this property?

13:16.158 --> 13:18.121
I am. I blew out my shoulder

13:18.206 --> 13:20.961
Playing minor league baseball,
so now I do this.

13:21.046 --> 13:24.050
<i>[announcer]
realtors: Never anyone's plan a.</i>

13:24.137 --> 13:25.681
And I also started
dating a woman

13:25.766 --> 13:28.269
Who looks like she actually
belongs with me.

13:28.396 --> 13:31.568
She has the most negative
dating app page I've ever seen.

13:31.654 --> 13:33.657
"wants to know where
all the good men are.

13:33.743 --> 13:36.873
Integrity only.
I will not cosign a loan,"

13:37.000 --> 13:38.294
With the "not" underlined.

13:38.338 --> 13:41.090
And a picture of her dog
that says, "the only man

13:41.176 --> 13:43.263
Who's never lied to me."
oh, this is great.

13:43.390 --> 13:46.687
Yeah, I think I'm a real
real guy now, peter.

13:46.815 --> 13:48.400
You sure are. You see, kev,

13:48.527 --> 13:50.321
Nothing's gonna stop you
in the real world

13:50.448 --> 13:53.078
Except for your own
cardiovascular system.

13:53.163 --> 13:55.500
Hey, I'm only heavy 'cause
adam sandler made me

13:55.586 --> 13:57.713
Gain 60 pounds
to be in his movies.

13:57.840 --> 13:59.510
I was ethel to his lucy.

13:59.637 --> 14:02.849
Anyway, I owe you, peter.
Put it there.

14:05.066 --> 14:06.986
Aah! What happened to your hand?

14:07.072 --> 14:10.995
I-I don't know.
It-it's disappearing.

14:11.080 --> 14:13.292
Were you also bit by brian?

14:13.378 --> 14:15.505
[laughs] that's the culkin.

14:22.189 --> 14:23.900
Let me guess,
one of you chuckleheads

14:24.028 --> 14:25.654
Has a nutcracker inside you.

14:25.741 --> 14:27.491
-What? No.
-Hi.

14:27.618 --> 14:30.040
We're nonjudgmental interns
just here to observe.

14:30.125 --> 14:31.459
False alarm. Not what I thought.

14:31.544 --> 14:33.088
[interns] aww.

14:33.174 --> 14:34.424
Whenever interns observe,

14:34.552 --> 14:35.845
It's because we think
you put something in there.

14:35.889 --> 14:38.727
Listen, doctor, I need you
to help my friend kevin.

14:38.812 --> 14:40.647
Oh, my god, kevin james!

14:40.733 --> 14:42.694
You know, you owe
your career to me.

14:42.780 --> 14:45.743
I'm the doctor who couldn't
save john candy.

14:45.828 --> 14:48.332
Doctor, my hand,
it's disappearing,

14:48.418 --> 14:50.253
And I don't know what to do.

14:51.258 --> 14:53.512
Kevin, your arm.
It's getting worse.

14:53.597 --> 14:56.309
Hmm. I think I see
what's going on here.

14:56.394 --> 14:57.688
Kevin is fading away

14:57.816 --> 14:59.901
Because streaming has
made him irrelevant.

15:00.071 --> 15:01.614
Is there anything
we can do for him?

15:01.699 --> 15:04.578
Yes. Sitcom stars like kevin
clearly need the laughs

15:04.664 --> 15:07.210
Of a studio audience,
or he may disappear forever.

15:07.255 --> 15:09.214
His hair was disappearing, too,

15:09.258 --> 15:11.345
But I assume he took care
of that another way.

15:11.430 --> 15:13.099
Is there someone I can talk to?

15:13.184 --> 15:15.814
Ah, there's our guy. Interns!

15:18.656 --> 15:21.076
Guys, we gotta get kevin
back on tv.

15:21.162 --> 15:22.413
So ideas. Go.

15:22.541 --> 15:24.250
Kevin plays a large robot,

15:24.377 --> 15:26.380
<i>And it's called big wonder.</i>

15:26.465 --> 15:28.510
[laughs] not bad, not bad.
Okay, what else?

15:28.638 --> 15:31.935
A show in which kevin moves in
with a woman named betsy,

15:32.021 --> 15:35.360
<i>And it's called kevins to betsy.</i>

15:35.446 --> 15:38.074
Or he's the seventh
in a long line of kevins,

15:38.160 --> 15:39.243
<i>For seventh kevin.</i>

15:39.330 --> 15:40.622
Yeah, they don't all
have to be puns

15:40.707 --> 15:42.000
Built around the name kevin.

15:42.085 --> 15:45.091
<i>Guys, I think we were all
laughing at big wonder.</i>

15:45.177 --> 15:46.344
<i>We're not doing big wonder.</i>

15:46.471 --> 15:48.390
Why? Because you didn't
think of it?

15:48.517 --> 15:51.439
Chris, the brainstorming process
is admittedly messy,

15:51.566 --> 15:53.360
But let's try to stay away
from personal attacks.

15:53.446 --> 15:56.869
I have an idea. I'm a stepdad
with six daughters,

15:56.955 --> 15:59.666
<i>And it's called daddy's girls.</i>

15:59.752 --> 16:01.295
I don't know.
Not sure I see the hook.

16:01.423 --> 16:04.427
And I trick them into
washing my car in their bikinis

16:04.555 --> 16:06.392
While I hide in the backseat.

16:06.477 --> 16:07.686
Okay, now I love it.

16:07.729 --> 16:09.774
It's not just funny, it's smart.

16:09.901 --> 16:11.235
You know, I'm on godaddy,

16:11.405 --> 16:14.118
And the domain name "big wonder"
is available.

16:14.245 --> 16:16.498
-Chris, stop pushing this.
-Oh, really?

16:16.583 --> 16:19.338
'cause if kevin pitched it,
you'd put your mouth on him.

16:19.465 --> 16:21.970
All right, that's it.
You're grounded for life.

16:22.097 --> 16:24.474
Which was also a fat dad sitcom.

16:24.560 --> 16:26.647
[laughs]
okay, all right, we've made up.

16:26.691 --> 16:29.069
I've got an idea.
Kevin is a baker,

16:29.196 --> 16:30.531
And he adopts 12 children.

16:30.616 --> 16:32.035
The title writes itself.

16:32.120 --> 16:34.875
Yeah, and the tagline is
"he's got muffin to lose."

16:34.960 --> 16:37.171
Okay, wow, all right,
this is too good for kevin.

16:37.256 --> 16:38.759
We have to write this now.

16:38.844 --> 16:41.766
<i>You know why he's a baker?
Because he kneads the dough.</i>

16:41.851 --> 16:45.483
[laughs] I love this poster.
I mean show.

16:45.568 --> 16:48.698
Peter, my arm is
almost gone now.

16:48.784 --> 16:50.285
Oh, god, what are we gonna do?

16:50.413 --> 16:51.831
Okay, come on, everyone.

16:51.917 --> 16:54.337
It's time to go to city hall
for the tree lighting.

16:54.422 --> 16:57.344
And meg's in the nativity play
as the virgin mary.

16:57.429 --> 16:59.725
Wait a minute.
The nativity play.

16:59.811 --> 17:03.234
Kevin, I got an idea,
and it's my best idea

17:03.361 --> 17:05.237
Since I put hockey ice
in the kitchen.

17:05.322 --> 17:07.618
-[timer dings]
-yay, waffles.

17:09.040 --> 17:11.585
Mine. Hockey house.

17:15.430 --> 17:17.349
Everyone, change of plans.

17:17.476 --> 17:18.644
This year we're gonna do a twist

17:18.729 --> 17:20.649
On the usual story
of the king of kings,

17:20.809 --> 17:23.989
With the "king of queens,"
kevin james.

17:27.374 --> 17:29.335
Peter, this isn't gonna work.

17:29.464 --> 17:30.755
Sure it will. The doctor said

17:30.799 --> 17:32.552
You need live audience laughter.

17:32.679 --> 17:35.349
The conceit is he's
a single dad with a baby.

17:35.435 --> 17:37.772
[laughs] the conception
may be immaculate,

17:37.816 --> 17:39.485
But the diaper sure isn't.

17:39.570 --> 17:41.907
-[booing]
-get off the stage.

17:41.993 --> 17:43.745
Network tv is stupid.

17:43.830 --> 17:46.250
Why does jerry stiller have
such a big chest?

17:46.336 --> 17:48.464
Peter, my leg.

17:50.471 --> 17:52.473
Come on, guys,
network tv isn't stupid.

17:52.558 --> 17:55.688
It-it's... It's like the bible.

17:55.816 --> 17:57.193
Sure, the plot doesn't
make sense

17:57.320 --> 17:58.404
If you think about it.

17:58.532 --> 17:59.866
The characters are a little
over the top.

17:59.952 --> 18:02.748
Both tell the same tired stories
again and again.

18:02.833 --> 18:04.710
No one ever seems
to learn their lesson.

18:04.796 --> 18:05.671
And neither ever offers

18:05.798 --> 18:07.425
An authentic female
point of view.

18:07.553 --> 18:09.137
Oh, if I can add to that--

18:09.223 --> 18:10.724
Not now, lois, I'm talking.

18:10.810 --> 18:13.731
But the point is, network tv...
It makes you feel good.

18:13.817 --> 18:16.697
And when the rest of life
is so exhausting and hard,

18:16.824 --> 18:19.328
Isn't that all that's important?

18:19.414 --> 18:20.915
Peter, my other leg!

18:21.919 --> 18:23.922
[soft laughter]

18:25.469 --> 18:27.013
Yes. Kevin, keep going.

18:27.098 --> 18:28.809
That went well.

18:28.894 --> 18:30.645
[laughter]

18:30.732 --> 18:32.651
Well, there's the star
of bethlehem,

18:32.737 --> 18:36.076
Which is one more star than
I'm giving this inn on yelp.

18:36.162 --> 18:37.455
[loud laughter]

18:37.540 --> 18:38.832
Oh, that's so funny.

18:38.917 --> 18:39.626
I use yelp.

18:39.795 --> 18:41.297
Do you think ben stiller's chest

18:41.382 --> 18:42.466
Will pop out like his dad's?

18:42.551 --> 18:44.220
I just want to know
what to expect.

18:44.306 --> 18:45.765
See, isn't this fun?

18:45.850 --> 18:48.480
Everyone laughing together
at the same simple thing,

18:48.608 --> 18:50.652
Instead of all of us
on our individual devices

18:50.779 --> 18:53.075
Watching depressing,
complicated bull crap?

18:53.160 --> 18:56.958
We need kevin james,
and we need network tv.

18:57.086 --> 18:59.130
<i>♪ joy to the world ♪</i>

18:59.257 --> 19:01.636
<i>♪ the lord is come ♪</i>

19:01.680 --> 19:06.272
<i>♪ let earth receive
 her king... ♪</i>

19:06.400 --> 19:09.113
Peter, my limbs.
They're coming back.

19:09.281 --> 19:11.618
And that's not all. Look!

19:14.501 --> 19:16.044
It's old sitcom stars.

19:16.171 --> 19:17.632
They're coming out
of the cornfield.

19:17.759 --> 19:19.886
It's jenna elfman.

19:20.013 --> 19:21.517
Tony danza.

19:21.602 --> 19:22.811
And, uh...

19:22.896 --> 19:25.567
<i>Traylor howard,
from two guys and a girl.</i>

19:25.695 --> 19:26.611
Yeah, you're not a star.

19:26.739 --> 19:27.865
You shouldn't be
in the cornfield.

19:27.992 --> 19:30.830
<i>But I was also in
the later seasons of monk.</i>

19:30.915 --> 19:32.082
I see.

19:32.168 --> 19:34.045
-[screaming]
-[splat]

19:34.132 --> 19:36.761
<i>Now your list of credits
includes castle.</i>

19:36.846 --> 19:38.806
Hi, I'm les moonves chen.

19:38.934 --> 19:41.145
And I'm hiding behind
my wife's name now.

19:41.272 --> 19:43.693
Kevin, I'm looking for
my own television comeback,

19:43.820 --> 19:46.951
And enough power that I can
sexually harass doctors again.

19:47.037 --> 19:49.582
-And I'm anyone else.
-I'll go with you.

19:49.626 --> 19:52.580
And to think I was
about to kiss you.

19:52.633 --> 19:55.010
Kevin, let's go make a sitcom.

19:55.180 --> 19:56.557
I can't believe it.

19:56.676 --> 19:58.602
I'm gonna be on tv again.

19:58.730 --> 20:01.652
I'm going back to hollywood.

20:02.949 --> 20:04.032
[all gasp]

20:07.542 --> 20:10.339
[gasps]
he's a christmas miracle.

20:10.424 --> 20:12.594
Can I please have
my tv back now?

20:12.680 --> 20:14.223
Yes, peter, you can.

20:14.350 --> 20:16.144
Yay! Kiss me, lois.

20:16.230 --> 20:18.233
And think about our marriage
while we're kissing.

20:18.360 --> 20:19.277
Mm...

20:19.362 --> 20:21.741
<i>♪ oh, barkley, my barkley ♪</i>

20:21.869 --> 20:23.871
<i>♪ the other dog we had. ♪</i>

20:29.386 --> 20:31.263
<i>And that's baker's dozen.</i>

20:31.390 --> 20:33.311
We're hoping you say yes.

20:33.396 --> 20:34.938
<i>Or just roll with it.</i>

20:35.065 --> 20:35.982
[laughter]

20:36.067 --> 20:37.361
Great pitch, guys.

20:37.447 --> 20:39.992
This is exactly the kind of
tagline-driven comedy

20:40.077 --> 20:41.746
-We're looking for.
-Really?

20:41.874 --> 20:44.126
The only problem is
we've already committed

20:44.211 --> 20:45.589
To another project:

20:45.674 --> 20:48.053
<i> -Big wonder.
-Thank you, gentlemen.</i>

20:48.096 --> 20:50.768
-What?!
-He owns the rights
to the domain name.

20:50.895 --> 20:52.396
That's a big deal in our world.

20:52.523 --> 20:53.690
Fine. We don't need you.

20:53.777 --> 20:56.447
We'll take this down the hall
to scott rudin.

20:56.574 --> 20:58.369
[loud crash]

20:58.455 --> 20:59.914
He threw a computer at me.

20:59.999 --> 21:02.253
He didn't even ask who I was.